# Optional. Leave everything empty (the default) and `make run` replays the hash-checked model cache: no model endpoint is
# contacted and no document text leaves the machine. The default converter mode is rules_only and needs no model at all.
#
# A live slice can score the Apertus pointer (review mode) over any vLLM-style OpenAI-compatible endpoint that serves
# Apertus. Forced choice needs the vLLM extras (continue_final_message + prompt_logprobs). The committed θ is valid only for
# the build it was fitted on (Public AI's `swiss-ai/apertus-v1.5-8b` name, which serves the 70B weights); Public AI was
# used for evaluation only, may route requests outside Switzerland and is not a runtime target. Example:
#   LLM_NAME=swiss-ai/apertus-v1.5-8b
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.publicai.co/v1
LLM_NAME=
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_API_KEY=
# GP_GGUF=1 scores the live slice locally with Apertus v1.5 8B GGUF Q4_K_M on CPU (5.1 GB download, sha256-pinned;
# build the image with `make run GGUF=1`); nothing leaves the machine.
GP_GGUF=0
